# HTTP controllers

Upwell 0.20 HTTP applications use the Axum integration and its controller macros. Define a DTO for the wire value, group endpoints with `#[controller]`, and mark route methods in `#[handlers]`.

<Example title="Expose a typed GET endpoint">

```rust plain
use upwell::axum::prelude::*;

#[dto]
struct Health {
    status: String,
}

#[controller(path = "/health")]
struct HealthController;
```

Add the handler to that controller:

```rust plain
#[handlers]
impl HealthController {
    #[get]
    async fn get(&self) -> Json<Health> {
        Json(Health {
            status: String::from("ok"),
        })
    }
}
```

</Example>

Register the controller through the 0.20 application builder and its Axum integration. Keep route shapes and generated HTTP behavior under the 0.20 release boundary; the current [HTTP controller guide](/docs/1.0.0/axum/http) is a 1.0 guide, not a compatibility statement for this release.
